--TEST--
`Core\Router\Match::attribute<T>()` with a `T` that is not a shape does not compile: `E0729` — `rule:routing/a-match-reads-an-attribute-as-data`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    #[Core\Route(path: "/shop", method: Core\Http\Method::Get)]
    #[Core\Access(allow: Core\Audience::Public)]
    #[{limit: 10}]
    public function index(): void {}
}

?Core\Router\Match $shop = Core\Router::match(Core\Http\Method::Get, "/shop");
?int $limit = $shop?->attribute<int>();
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0729]: `Core\Router\Match::attribute` returns an attribute by its shape, and `int` is not a shape
   --> case.nvs:10:15
   |
10 | ?int $limit = $shop?->attribute<int>();
   |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `int` written here
   = help: write a shape such as `{ seconds: int }`, or a `type` name for one. An attribute matches when it has every field of the shape

error: aborting due to 1 error
